---
title: White Sandwich Bread
description: Two soft sandwich loaves from an instant-yeast dough that rests 10 minutes and rises only once.
tags: [bread, baking]
course: side
icons: [wheat, sandwich, oven]
cuisine: American
source:
  name: Crazy for Crust
  author: Dorothy Kern
  url: https://www.crazyforcrust.com/easy-white-bread/
servings: 24
yield: 2%loaves
time: 2h
---

> **Yeast** — Use instant yeast (RapidRise is one brand), not active dry, and check the date on the packet.

Combine the @all-purpose flour{248%g}(2 cups to start, spooned and leveled), @granulated sugar{37%g}(3 tbsp), @instant yeast{14%g}(2 packets, 4 1/2 tsp), and @salt{2%tsp} in the bowl of a #stand mixer{} and stir until blended.

Combine the @water{1 1/2%cup}(355 ml), @milk{1/2%cup}(118 ml), and @butter{28%g}(2 tbsp, at room temperature) in a #microwave-safe bowl{}. Microwave on high in 15-second bursts until very warm but not hot to the touch, 120 to 130°F (49 to 54°C) on an #instant-read thermometer{}. The butter won't melt completely. Add to the flour mixture.

> **Swaps** — Honey works in place of the sugar, in the same amount. Any milk works, dairy or not. Oil, coconut oil, or margarine can stand in for the butter.

Beat with the dough hook at medium speed for ~beat{2%minutes}, scraping the bowl occasionally. Add 1 cup of the remaining @&all-purpose flour{124%g} and beat at high speed for ~beat{2%minutes}, scraping the bowl occasionally.

Stir in just enough of the remaining @&all-purpose flour{372%g} that the dough forms a ball and pulls away from the sides of the bowl, 2 1/2 to 3 cups. You may not need the last 1/2 cup.

> **By Hand** — No mixer needed. Stir the warm liquid into the dry ingredients in a large bowl with a wooden spoon until you can't stir anymore, then turn the shaggy dough out and knead.

Knead on a lightly floured surface until the dough is smooth and elastic and springs back when lightly pressed with 2 fingers, ~knead{6-8%minutes}. Cover with a #towel{} and let rest for ~rest{10%minutes}.

Cut the dough into 2 equal pieces. With a #rolling pin{}, roll each piece into a 12-by-7-inch rectangle.

Starting at a short end, roll each rectangle up tightly. Pinch the seams and ends to seal. Place the loaves seam side down in two #loaf pans{}(8 1/2 by 4 1/2 inches) coated with nonstick cooking spray. Cover with the towel and let rise in a warm place until doubled in size, about ~rise{45%minutes}. Meanwhile, heat the oven to 400°F (200°C) with a rack in the center.

Bake until golden brown and 190°F (88°C) in the center, ~bake{20-30%minutes}. Run a knife around the edges of the pans and turn the loaves out onto a #wire rack{} to cool.

> **Storing** — Keeps on the counter for 2 to 3 days. To freeze the second loaf, cool it completely, then wrap it in plastic wrap.
